# Operating — Local Environment (PRIVATE; fill in, do not publish)

Copy this file to `OPERATING.local.md` in your PRIVATE deployment mirror
and fill in the values. The deployment agent reads it alongside
`OPERATING.md` for environment specifics that must NOT appear in the
public repo. `OPERATING.local.md` is gitignored here so a filled copy is
never pushed to the public repo by accident — keep it only in the
private mirror.

Keep this SHORT and factual. These are stable facts, not behavioral
rules (the rules live in `OPERATING.md`, which is durable and pulled).
Do not restate operating discipline here.

## CI / repo

- CI platform: Azure DevOps (pipelines under `pipelines/` are the
  reference; the live definitions are in the private mirror).
- The `az` CLI is installed and authenticated for this environment. Use
  it for repo/pipeline interaction per the patterns the pipelines use
  (REST + `System.AccessToken` for PRs; never interactive `az` calls
  that wait on stdin — see `pipelines/commitback.sh`).
- Azure DevOps org URL: <fill in, e.g. https://dev.azure.com/your-org>
- Project / repo name: <fill in>

## Credentials (NAMES ONLY — never the secret values)

- Variable group holding Zscaler API credentials: <fill in name>
- Backend (state) config file the pipelines pass: <fill in, e.g.
  backend.conf>
- Proxied egress? If yes, the env var the steps set: <e.g. HTTPS_PROXY>
  (curl/terraform read it from the env; a missing declaration is a
  classic "pushed the branch then hung" cause).

